  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper formulates two QUBO encodings for Max-Sharpe portfolio optimization on 432 S&P 500 assets, using 3888 and 5184 binary variables with 9-bit and 12-bit discretizations, respectively, and solves them via D-Wave QBSolv and D-Wave Hybrid with calibrated penalty parameters (e.g., λ₀≈1.2631 or 0.7, λ₁=300). It reports feasibility rates over grids of λ₀–λ₁ pairs (20 runs per pair) and collects 10 feasible solutions per configuration, comparing Sharpe ratio distributions and asset counts to a PyPortfolioOpt classical baseline, but does not demonstrate a clear performance advantage over the classical method.",
